    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d486">

                <pb facs="0690" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg616"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Washburn.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 57.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 21, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch No. 70, written at Buenos
                    Ayres on the 20th of September last, has been received,</p>
                <p>I thank you for the information it contains in regard to the operations of the
                    war in South America between the allied states and Paraguay.</p>
                <p>I learn from your communication that so late as the day of its date you were
                    still remaining outside of the country to which you are accredited.</p>
                <p>I have nothing to add to what was said in my No. 56 in regard to that painful
                    subject, which despatch is now, for the sake of caution, duplicated.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD,</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chales A. Washburn,</hi> Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
